    "references": [
      {
        "link": "https://digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT20-016#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official JP Q&A for BT20-016 (2025/01/24, translated by DeepL)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it is possible.",
        "question": "Can I not attack with this card after this card's [On Play] [When Digivolving] effect grants \"Penetrating\" and DP+4000 to one of my Digimon?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you cannot attack. While attacking, you cannot declare a new attack. In this situation, you can attack with \"BT16-077 Dino Beamon\" under the [When Digivolving] effect of \"BT16-077 Dino Beamon\". Before the Counter timing, the card's [On Play] and [When Digivolving] effects can be activated, but you cannot declare an attack during the attack, so you cannot attack even if you activate it.",
        "question": "With the [When Digivolving] effect of \"BT16-077 Dinobeamon\", I played this card [On Play] and attacked a player with \"BT16-077 Dinobeamon\" with \"Quick Attack\" as it is. After that, can I attack with this card by its [On Play] [When Digivolving] effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, they do not leave the Battle Area. DNA digivolves digivolve as a new Digimon, so it is a different Digimon than the one that leaves.",
        "question": "If this card's [All Turns] effect is activated and two Digimon including the leaving Digimon digivolve, does the digivolved Digimon leave the Battle Area?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
